# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: Lumen, from its release zip Lumen.zip.
Package: Lumen
Section: Graphics
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Suggests: LumenRaw, LumenHEIF, LumenLens
Components: Apps.Graphics.!Lumen (Movable LookAt)
Description: Photo library and non-destructive editor
 Lumen imports, browses, rates, flags and adjusts photos without
 changing them: white balance, exposure, highlights and shadows,
 levels, curves, contrast, saturation, sharpening, noise reduction,
 lens correction, crop, straighten and perspective, layers (brushes,
 gradients and ovals) and retouching, with presets, undo, a loupe and
 a 100% view; then exports them as JPEG, PNG or TIFF. One window with a
 browser, viewer, split view and full screen, and a scratch
 directory that keeps raw photos developed at full size.
 .
 Camera raw files need the LibRaw plug-in (LumenRaw), HEIF and AVIF
 photos the LumenHEIF plug-in, and lens profiles the LumenLens plug-in:
 separate packages.
Build-Map: !Lumen -> Apps/Graphics/!Lumen
